# You design and build LEGO Technic models one step at a time, in a build language.
#
# For each step you write:
# ADD name partnumber color
# CONNECT part.point -> part.point LOCKED|TURNS|STIFF   (points: hole1.., axlehole1.., pin1.., axle1.., clip1..; LOCKED = cross in cross, turn together; TURNS = free; STIFF = friction pin)
# Optional: MESH a.teeth b.teeth / RATIO a b x/y / GROUP g (opens a side build) / END (closes it) / ATTACH g (joins a finished side build into the main model)
# WHY one plain sentence: what this step builds and what it is for.
# A point ending in ~ is an estimate; ? means not known.
#
# Rules: only use real points of each part; a round pin never goes in a cross hole; a shaft that must turn needs round holes; a worm needs stops on both sides; gears must sit at the right distance.
STEP 1
ADD hub-1 32184 black
ADD hub-axle-1 4519 lightgray
ADD hub-pin-1 2780 black
CONNECT hub-axle-1.axle1 -> hub-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT hub-pin-1.pin1 -> hub-1.hole1 STIFF
WHY Starts the chassis spine with a cross connector, a locked axle through it and a friction pin for the next part to hang on.

STEP 2
ADD hub-2 32184 black
ADD hub-bush-1 3713 lightgray
CONNECT hub-pin-1.pin2 -> hub-2.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT hub-axle-1.axle2 -> hub-bush-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
WHY Extends the spine with a second cross connector and caps the axle end with a bush so it can't slide out.

STEP 3
ADD hub-pin-2 2780 black
ADD hub-conn2-1 60483 darkgray
CONNECT hub-pin-2.pin1 -> hub-2.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT hub-conn2-1.hole1 -> hub-pin-2.pin2 STIFF
WHY Adds a beam with a pin and axle hole off the spine, the start of the engine cowling frame.

STEP 4
ADD body-beam11-1 32525 black
ADD body-pin-1 2780 black
ADD body-pin-2 2780 black
CONNECT body-pin-1.pin1 -> hub-1.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT body-pin-2.pin1 -> hub-2.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT body-beam11-1.hole1 -> body-pin-1.pin2 STIFF
CONNECT body-beam11-1.hole11 -> body-pin-2.pin2 STIFF
WHY Lays an 11-hole beam across both cross connectors to start the left chassis rail.

STEP 5
ADD body-beam11-2 32525 black
ADD body-pin-3 2780 black
ADD body-pin-4 2780 black
CONNECT body-pin-3.pin1 -> hub-1.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT body-pin-4.pin1 -> hub-2.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT body-beam11-2.hole1 -> body-pin-3.pin2 STIFF
CONNECT body-beam11-2.hole11 -> body-pin-4.pin2 STIFF
WHY Mirrors the first rail on the other side of the spine so the chassis is symmetric.

STEP 6
ADD body-lshape-1 32140 black
ADD body-lshape-2 32140 black
WHY Hangs an L-shaped beam off each rail to start turning the frame upward toward the engine cover.

STEP 7
ADD body-axle-1 32073 lightgray
ADD body-conn-1 32039 lightgray
CONNECT body-axle-1.axle1 -> body-lshape-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT body-conn-1.axlehole1 -> body-axle-1.axle2 LOCKED
WHY Runs a 5L axle between the two L-beams so they hold their angle and share a common cross-brace.

STEP 8
ADD body-axle-2 32073 lightgray
ADD body-conn-2 32039 lightgray
CONNECT body-axle-2.axle1 -> body-lshape-2.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT body-conn-2.axlehole1 -> body-axle-2.axle2 LOCKED
WHY Mirrors the cross-brace on the other side, squaring up the upper frame.

STEP 9
ADD body-bent-1 32271 black
ADD body-pin-5 2780 black
ADD body-pin-6 2780 black
CONNECT body-pin-5.pin1 -> body-beam11-1.hole9~ STIFF
CONNECT body-pin-6.pin1 -> body-beam11-2.hole9~ STIFF
CONNECT body-bent-1.hole1 -> body-pin-5.pin2 STIFF
WHY Adds a 7-3 bent beam at the rear of one rail to begin the kick-up toward the tail of the hood.

STEP 10
ADD body-bent-2 32271 black
CONNECT body-bent-2.hole1 -> body-pin-6.pin2 STIFF
WHY Mirrors the rear kick-up beam on the other rail.

STEP 11
ADD str-conn-1 92907 black
ADD str-axle-1 4519 lightgray
CONNECT str-axle-1.axle1 -> body-conn-1.axlehole2 LOCKED
CONNECT str-conn-1.axlehole1 -> str-axle-1.axle2 LOCKED
WHY Builds the start of the steering column off the front cross-brace.

STEP 12
ADD str-conn-2 92907 black
ADD str-pin-1 2780 black
CONNECT str-pin-1.pin1 -> str-conn-1.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT str-conn-2.hole1~ -> str-pin-1.pin2 STIFF
WHY Stacks a second perpendicular split connector to carry the steering linkage higher.

STEP 13
ADD str-conn-4 32184 black
WHY Stacks another cross connector on the steering tower for the handlebar linkage to pick up later.

STEP 14
ADD str-arm-1 15459 lightgray
ADD str-arm-2 15459 lightgray
ADD str-gear-1 15460 darkgray
WHY Builds the steering gear with a towball steering arm on each side, the core of the Ackermann linkage.

STEP 15
ADD str-ball-1 2736 lightgray
ADD str-ball-2 2736 lightgray
CONNECT str-ball-1.axle1 -> str-conn-1.axlehole2~ LOCKED
CONNECT str-ball-2.axle1 -> str-conn-2.axlehole2~ LOCKED
WHY Adds the two towballs that the steering arms will clip onto, letting the skis swivel.

STEP 16
ADD str-conn-3 15461 black
CONNECT str-conn-3.hole1 -> str-axle-1.axle3~ TURNS
WHY Adds a 3L pin connector on the steering column so the handlebar mast can be plugged in above it.

STEP 17
GROUP gearbox
ADD gb-frame-1 32526 white
ADD gb-frame-2 32526 white
ADD gb-conn-1 32184 black
ADD gb-conn-2 32184 black
ADD gb-axle-1 3706 black
ADD gb-axle-2 3706 black
ADD gb-gear-1 87407 lightgray
ADD gb-gear-2 87407 lightgray
ADD gb-gear-3 87407 lightgray
ADD gb-gear-4 87407 lightgray
ADD gb-stop-1 87083 darkgray
ADD gb-stop-2 87083 darkgray
ADD gb-axlepin-1 32062 red
ADD gb-axlepin-2 32062 red
CONNECT gb-gear-1.hole1 -> gb-axle-1.axle2 TURNS
CONNECT gb-gear-2.hole1 -> gb-axle-1.axle3~ TURNS
CONNECT gb-gear-3.hole1 -> gb-axle-2.axle2 TURNS
CONNECT gb-gear-4.hole1 -> gb-axle-2.axle3~ TURNS
CONNECT gb-axlepin-1.axle1 -> gb-gear-1.hole1~ TURNS
CONNECT gb-axlepin-2.axle1 -> gb-gear-3.hole1~ TURNS
MESH gb-gear-1.teeth gb-gear-2.teeth
MESH gb-gear-3.teeth gb-gear-4.teeth
END gearbox
ATTACH gearbox
WHY Builds the bevel-gear track sprocket shafts as their own unit before dropping them into the chassis; Attaches the finished sprocket-shaft unit under the chassis rails where the track will wrap around it.

STEP 18
ADD trk-beam11-1 32525 black
ADD trk-pin-1 2780 black
CONNECT trk-pin-1.pin1 -> body-beam11-1.hole11~ STIFF
CONNECT trk-beam11-1.hole1 -> trk-pin-1.pin2 STIFF
WHY Extends the rail rearward with another 11-hole beam to carry the length of the track run.

STEP 19
ADD trk-beam7-1 32524 lime
ADD trk-beam5-1 32316 black
ADD trk-pin-2 2780 black
CONNECT trk-pin-2.pin1 -> trk-beam11-1.hole7~ STIFF
CONNECT trk-beam7-1.hole1 -> trk-pin-2.pin2 STIFF
WHY Adds the lime side panel beams that will show through the track guard.

STEP 20
ADD trk-pinconn-1 15461 black
CONNECT trk-pinconn-1.pin1 -> trk-beam5-1.hole5~ STIFF
WHY Adds a 3L pin connector at the end of the side panel for the rear mudguard to clip onto later.

STEP 21
ADD trk-axlepin-1 32062 red
ADD trk-axlepin-2 32062 red
WHY Extends both sprocket axles out to the rear idler position with notched red axles.

STEP 22
ADD trk-conn-1 92907 black
ADD trk-conn-2 92907 black
CONNECT trk-conn-1.axlehole1 -> trk-axlepin-1.axle2~ LOCKED
CONNECT trk-conn-2.axlehole1 -> trk-axlepin-2.axle2~ LOCKED
WHY Caps the rear idler axles with perpendicular split connectors so the track loop has somewhere to turn.

STEP 23
ADD body-panel-1 11946 black
ADD body-panel-2 11947 black
WHY Applies the left and right 5L side-fairing panels over the chassis rails, carrying stickers 5 and 9.

STEP 24
ADD body-panel-3 11946 black
ADD body-panel-4 11947 black
ADD body-link-1 32005a black
CONNECT body-link-1.pin1 -> trk-beam7-1.hole3~ STIFF
WHY Continues the fairing panels rearward and adds a short link track guide, carrying stickers 3 and 6.

STEP 25
ADD trk-tread-1 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-2 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-3 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-4 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-5 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-6 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-7 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-8 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-9 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-10 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-11 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-12 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-13 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-14 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-15 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-16 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-17 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-18 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-19 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-20 15379 black
WHY Wraps the first run of beveled tread links around the sprocket and idler; the tread tension holds the loop together without a separate join.

STEP 26
ADD trk-tread-21 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-22 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-23 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-24 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-25 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-26 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-27 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-28 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-29 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-30 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-31 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-32 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-33 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-34 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-35 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-36 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-37 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-38 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-39 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-40 15379 black
ADD trk-tread-41 15379 black
ADD body-shock-1 76138 lightgray
WHY Finishes the first track loop and fits a soft-spring shock absorber between the rail and the sprocket frame to cushion the ride.

STEP 27
GROUP ski-left
ADD skiL-angle-1 32016 black
ADD skiL-pin-1 2780 black
ADD skiL-ski-1 14720 lightgray
CONNECT skiL-pin-1.pin1 -> skiL-angle-1.hole1 STIFF
CONNECT skiL-ski-1.hole1~ -> skiL-pin-1.pin2 STIFF
END ski-left
ATTACH ski-left
CONNECT skiL-angle-1.axlehole1~ -> str-ball-1.axle1 LOCKED
WHY Builds the left ski's angled mounting arm so the ski can pivot under spring load; Fits the left ski arm onto the steering towball so turning the handlebars steers the ski.

STEP 28
GROUP ski-right
ADD skiR-angle-1 32016 black
ADD skiR-pin-1 2780 black
ADD skiR-ski-1 60483 darkgray
CONNECT skiR-pin-1.pin1 -> skiR-angle-1.hole1 STIFF
CONNECT skiR-ski-1.hole1~ -> skiR-pin-1.pin2 STIFF
END ski-right
ATTACH ski-right
CONNECT skiR-angle-1.axlehole1~ -> str-ball-2.axle1 LOCKED
WHY Mirrors the ski arm for the right side with a beam forming the ski's tip mount; Fits the right ski arm onto its towball so both skis steer together.

STEP 29
ADD trim-link-1 32005a black
ADD trim-beam13-1 41239 lime
ADD trim-beam13-2 41239 lime
ADD trim-tooth-1 41669 transclear
ADD trim-tooth-2 41669 transclear
ADD trim-beam3x0.5-1 33299b black
ADD trim-beam3x0.5-2 33299b black
ADD trim-bent-1 32009 black
ADD trim-bent-2 32009 black
ADD trim-beam3thin-1 6632 white
ADD trim-beam3thin-2 6632 white
ADD trim-hub-1 57585 lightgray
ADD trim-conn-1 59443 lightgray
ADD trim-axle3-1 4519 lightgray
ADD trim-axle3-2 4519 lightgray
ADD trim-pinhalf-1 4274 lightgray
ADD trim-axlepin-1 3749 tan
ADD trim-pinlong-1 32556 tan
ADD trim-pinlong-2 32556 tan
ADD trim-pin-1 3673 lightgray
ADD trim-pin-2 3673 lightgray
ADD trim-pin-3 3673 lightgray
ADD trim-pin-4 3673 lightgray
ADD trim-pin-5 3673 lightgray
ADD trim-pin-6 3673 lightgray
ADD trim-long-1 6558 blue
ADD trim-long-2 6558 blue
ADD trim-long-3 6558 blue
ADD trim-long-4 6558 blue
ADD trim-long-5 6558 blue
ADD trim-long-6 6558 blue
ADD trim-long-7 6558 blue
ADD trim-long-8 6558 blue
ADD trim-long-9 6558 blue
ADD trim-stopbush-1 32054 black
ADD trim-stopbush-2 32054 black
ADD trim-stopbush-3 32054 black
ADD trim-stopbush-4 32054 black
ADD trim-11214-1 11214 darkgray
ADD trim-11214-2 11214 darkgray
ADD trim-bush-1 3713 lightgray
ADD trim-bush-2 3713 lightgray
ADD trim-lshape-1 32140 lime
ADD trim-lshape-2 32140 lime
ADD trim-lshape-3 32140 lime
ADD trim-lshape-4 32140 lime
ADD trim-panel-1 32526 white
ADD trim-panel-3 11946 black
ADD trim-panel-4 11947 black
ADD trim-arm-3 15459 lightgray
ADD trim-arm-4 15459 lightgray
ADD trim-gear-2 15460 darkgray
ADD trim-aconn-1 32039 lightgray
ADD trim-aconn-2 32039 lightgray
ADD trim-axle5-1 32073 lightgray
ADD trim-beam5-1 32316 black
ADD trim-beam5-2 32316 black
ADD trim-beam5-3 32316 black
ADD trim-beam7-1 32524 lime
ADD trim-beam11-1 32525 black
ADD trim-conn2-1 60483 darkgray
ADD trim-conn2-2 60483 darkgray
ADD trim-shock-1 76138 lightgray
ADD trim-astop-1 87083 darkgray
ADD trim-notched-1 32062 red
ADD trim-notched-2 32062 red
ADD trim-notched-3 32062 red
ADD trim-notched-4 32062 red
ADD trim-notched-5 32062 red
ADD trim-notched-6 32062 red
ADD trim-notched-7 32062 red
ADD trim-notched-8 32062 red
ADD trim-notched-9 32062 red
ADD trim-notched-10 32062 red
CONNECT trim-hub-1.axle1~ -> trim-conn-1.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT trim-aconn-1.axlehole1~ -> trim-axle5-1.axle1 LOCKED
CONNECT trim-aconn-2.axlehole1~ -> trim-axle5-1.axle2~ LOCKED
CONNECT trim-notched-1.axle1 -> trim-conn2-1.axlehole1~ LOCKED
CONNECT trim-notched-2.axle1 -> trim-conn2-2.axlehole1~ LOCKED
WHY Fills in the handlebar mast, windshield frame, headlight trim, the second shock absorber and the remaining fairing panels and spare axles, then finishes with stickers 1, 2 and 10 to complete the model.
